 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Not really. It's a good way to see how it looks in different lighting. Do want show it off in living room with big windows, or keep it somewhere dark with a little light box? Then maybe start a fresh Facebook group where the only rule is everyone shares only their own artwork. You could even call it something playful like art spotters. You' get better fast by practicing and looking at critiques. Tracing a photo gives you a good likeness right away, which can give you a false sense of progress. Go both ways for a while, and you' see which one gives you joy. Whichever one that is, push that button.",
